.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rev-stealth-config-get 1  "rev-stealth-config-get " 
.SH NAME
rev\-stealth\-config\-get \- Resolve a dotted key path (e.g. `policy.require_vpn`) against the merged config and print the value. Secret\-looking values redacted
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrev\-stealth config get\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIKEY\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Resolve a dotted key (e.g. `policy.require_vpn`, `env.VPN_INSTANCES`) against the merged effective config. Secret\-looking values are replaced with `<redacted>`.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIKEY\fR>
Dotted key, e.g. `policy.require_vpn` or `env.VPN_INSTANCES`
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  $ rev\-stealth config get policy.require_vpn
  $ rev\-stealth config get env.VPN_INSTANCES
  $ rev\-stealth config \-\-output\-format json get policy.require_vpn

EXIT CODES:
  0  Ok               Value emitted.
  1  UserError        Bad key / unknown path.
  3  PermanentError   Config IO / parse failure.

ENV:
  REV_SCRAPING_HOME        Override `~/.rev_scraping/` base.
  REV_SCRAPING_POLICY      Override the policy.toml path.
  REV_SCRAPING_AUTHORIZED  Override the authorized.toml path.
